.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt VM_STAT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vm_stat
.Nd show virtual memory statistics
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Oo Fl c Ar count Oc Ar interval
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the kernel's virtual memory statistics, in pages of the size its
first line gives: free, active, inactive, speculative, throttled, wired
and purgeable pages; page faults, copy-on-write and zero-filled pages,
reactivated and purged pages; file-backed and anonymous pages; the pages
stored in and taken by the compressor, decompressions and compressions;
page-ins, page-outs, swap-ins and swap-outs.
.Pp
With an
.Ar interval
in seconds, it prints them as a table every
.Ar interval
seconds: the first row has the totals, the next ones what changed since
the row before (the page counts are always as they are now).
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar count
Stop after
.Ar count
rows.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr top 1
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
